        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(durable): wire agent session runtime coordination",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThis PR wires the durable runtime foundation from PR2 into agent/session/subagent paths so OpenClaw can record durable context for chat sends, agent runs, subagent child runs, parent fan-in, yield progress, and restart/recovery inspection.\n\nThe target behavior is: parent agents should have durable child/fan-in state; one failed child should not make sibling completion invisible; and Gateway/session restart should leave inspectable runtime state instead of silent coordinator ambiguity.\n\n## Dependency Chain\n\nThis is PR3 in the replacement durable runtime stack:\n\n1. PR1: durable session/task runtime RFC v2.\n2. PR2: durable runtime foundation.\n3. PR3: agent/session/subagent wiring, this PR.\n\nThis branch is stacked on the PR2 branch. The upstream PR diff against `main` is therefore cumulative. For delta-only review after PR2, use:\n\nhttps://github.com/mjnkao/openclaw/compare/codex/openclaw-durable-runtime-foundation-v2-ready...codex/openclaw-durable-runtime-agent-v2-ready\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds:\n\n- Gateway `chat.send` and `agent.run` durable context refs;\n- user-turn transcript durable context propagation;\n- embedded-agent yield progress for resumable parent turns;\n- subagent child-run mirroring and parent fan-in association;\n- task completion contract metadata for durable parent/child lifecycle;\n- status-notice display metadata for durable/yield progress;\n- protocol schema fields for durable context references.\n\nReview follow-up:\n\n- Restores the existing `/pair qr` sensitive-display path so WebChat still broadcasts an `openclaw_pairing_qr` block without persisting QR content into transcripts.\n- Carries the latest PR2 disabled-CLI no-mutation fix in this stacked branch.\n\n## Explicit Non-Scope\n\n- Work module.\n- Workboard UI/tools.\n- Task Flow projection adapters.\n- Retention/compaction.\n- Postgres/multi-worker lease contention.\n- Durable write controls such as cancel/retry/resume/signal.\n\n## Evidence\n\nReview follow-up validation after ClawSweeper feedback:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway.config.ts src/gateway/server-methods/chat.directive-tags.test.ts`\n  - 2 files, 262 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts src/durable/fan-in.test.ts src/durable/subagent.test.ts src/durable/agent-turn.test.ts`\n  - 3 files, 14 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.commands.config.ts src/commands/durable.test.ts`\n  - 1 file, 2 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway.config.ts src/gateway/server-methods/durable.test.ts`\n  - 2 files, 4 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/generate-docs-map.mjs --check` passed.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\nFocused validation observed locally:\n\n- Gateway/context/server-methods shard:\n  - 6 files, 176 tests passed.\n- Agent tools shard:\n  - 2 files, 67 tests passed.\n- Agent/session/task policy shard:\n  - 1 file, 27 tests passed.\n- Durable fan-in/subagent/agent-turn shard:\n  - 3 files, 14 tests passed.\n- Exact durable matrix from the previous durable-core PR:\n  - 6 files, 36 tests passed.\n- Exact Gateway durable matrix:\n  - 2 files, 4 tests passed.\n  - Covers enabled projection and disabled read paths that do not create durable SQLite state.\n- Shared-state permissions/query-plan matrix:\n  - 3 files, 26 tests passed, 1 skipped.\n- Subagent lifecycle compatibility:\n  - 1 file, 8 tests passed.\n- Redaction/bounded metadata regression:\n  - `src/durable/subagent.test.ts` verifies `taskHash` is stored and raw `task` is not stored on child run or parent link metadata.\n- `node scripts/generate-kysely-types.mjs --verify` passed.\n- `node scripts/check-kysely-guardrails.mjs` passed with `Kysely guardrails OK`.\n- `npm run tsgo:core` passed.\n- `npm run tsgo:core:test` passed.\n- `OPENCLAW_LOCAL_CHECK=0 node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.core.test.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core-test.tsbuildinfo` passed.\n- `npm run tsgo:prod` passed after `pnpm tsgo:core && pnpm tsgo:extensions`.\n- `./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 <changed durable/state/gateway files>` passed on 62 files.\n- `node --import tsx /private/tmp/openclaw-durable-runtime-proof.mts` passed against an isolated temporary SQLite database:\n  - created 3 runtime runs, 2 timeline events, and 1 fan-in step;\n  - projected 2 child runs with 1 succeeded, 1 failed, 2 terminal, and 0 open;\n  - projected reportable `lost` recovery state for restart/reconciliation proof.\n\n## Local Build Note\n\n`env CI=true npm run build` was attempted locally. Dependency installation and bundled plugin assets completed, then the root `tsdown` build emitted only heartbeat lines for more than ten minutes and was manually interrupted. This is not recorded as passing build proof; CI or a maintainer machine should still run the full build before merge.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis PR replaces the agent/session/subagent wiring portion of #97508 with runtime-oriented naming and a narrower dependency chain.\n",
